description:
FILED s543a (Opus, 2026-11-16), found by the line-track flip's probe 2 (scratch/s543a/probes/p2-die.pl row 9a in the s543a worktree).

perl 5.40.3 gives an `elsif` CONDITION its own statement location (a nextstate before the condition), so a runtime die raised while evaluating it names the elsif's line.  PCL writes one `(p-line N)` per statement, and an if/elsif/else chain is ONE statement whose line is the `if`'s.

PROBE:
   33 eval {
   34     if ($z > 5) {
   35         1;
   36     } elsif (1 / $z) {
   37         2;
   38     }
   39 }; print $@;
  perl: Illegal division by zero at F line 36.
  PCL : Illegal division by zero at F line 34.

A multi-line `if` CONDITION reports the if's first line in both (perl 41 = PCL 41, row 9b), and a `while` condition the while line (row 10) -- only elsif differs.  Fix shape (not built): the elsif arm's condition lowered as `(progn (p-line M) COND)` when M differs from the chain's line (Parser2 `_lower_compound`'s if arm).  Cost: one store per elsif condition evaluated.  Also check `unless ... elsif`, and `caller` from a sub called in the elsif condition (the same register).
